     </HEAD>
     <LINES>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>&amp;DEFINITION&amp;</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Test data container variants (TDCV) store the test data required to</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>perform the defined action for the defined business object.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>The data structure behind a TDCV depends on the chosen business object</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>and action. There may be combinations of business objects and actions</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>where a TDCV is not necessary, for example when creating an invoice for</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>an order. In cases like this, you need to create a reference step to</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>define the business object the system is to use as predecessor.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>&amp;USE&amp;</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>&amp;DEPENDENCIES&amp;</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>&amp;EXAMPLE&amp;</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>To create a debit memo request, the system requires certain data such as</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>the customer, material, and so on. Using a TDCV, you can store the</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>required information.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>&amp;NOTE&amp;</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
       <TDLINE>Should you require additional or different test data, create additional</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
      <TLINE>
       <TDLINE>TDCVs using transaction &lt;ZH&gt;secatt&lt;/&gt;.</TDLINE>
      </TLINE>
     </LINES>
    </item>
